    {
      "label": "Lonely man is burying a coffin",
      "color": "#a55faa",
      "value": 1,
      "title": "\n            <body>\n            <h3> <a href='https://nicholascorniaorpheus.github.io/a_gothic_gamebook/scenes/Lonely_man_is_burying_a_coffin_-_AGG_2025'>Lonely man is burying a coffin</a></h3>\n            <p>Amidst the ruins, Rune is woken by the faint light of dawn. From one of the surviving gothic windows, Rune sees a lonely figure digging a deep hole in the nearby graveyard. Rune decides to ask the only living being in the castle for directions. Musical pieces: Die alten, bösen Lieder Op. 48 no. 16</p>\n            </body>\n            ",
      "music": [],
      "public_choice": false,
      "id": 12
    },
    {
      "label": "Meeting the Witch",
      "color": "#a55faa",
      "value": 1,
      "title": "\n            <body>\n            <h3> <a href='https://nicholascorniaorpheus.github.io/a_gothic_gamebook/scenes/Meeting_the_Witch_-_AGG_2025'>Meeting the Witch</a></h3>\n            <p>After a night spent wandering, the dawn begins to break. A flock of crows suddenly darkens the early morning sky, and then disperses, leaving only a single bird behind. Sasha has the feeling that this bird is looking back at them with almost human intelligence. Musical pieces: Sehnsucht D.123</p>\n            </body>\n            ",
