    {
      "label": "Reaching higher ground during a storm",
      "color": "#a55faa",
      "value": 1,
      "title": "\n            <body>\n            <h3> <a href='https://nicholascorniaorpheus.github.io/a_gothic_gamebook/scenes/Reaching_higher_ground_during_a_storm_-_AGG_2025'>Reaching higher ground during a storm</a></h3>\n            <p>Rain has been falling incessantly since Sasha’s departure. The path is inaccessible, and Sasha has lost their way. Their only chance is to climb the nearest hill in order to attain a new sense of orientation. Fighting against the rain and wind, Sasha realises that the storm is intensifying. Musical pieces: Stürmisch Wandern, Op. 18 n.°6</p>\n            </body>\n            ",
      "music": [],
      "public_choice": true,
      "id": 17
    },
    {
      "label": "Recognition of the evil sorceress",
      "color": "#a55faa",
      "value": 1,
      "title": "\n            <body>\n            <h3> <a href='https://nicholascorniaorpheus.github.io/a_gothic_gamebook/scenes/Recognition_of_the_evil_sorceress_-_AGG_2025'>Recognition of the evil sorceress</a></h3>\n            <p>After being hit by the pebble, the strange bird emits a sharp sound like a woman’s scream. Is it possible? Instead of a bird, Sasha is confronted by a furious witch with pale skin and scarlet curls. Shrieking curses in an unknown language, the figure approaches. Sasha runs away as fast as possible.Musical pieces: Waldesgespräch, op. 39 no. 3</p>\n            </body>\n            ",
      "music": [],
      "public_choice": false,
      "id": 18
    },
    {
      "label": "Sad ending",
      "color": "#c14834",
      "value": 10,
      "title": "\n            <body>\n            <h3> <a href='https://nicholascorniaorpheus.github.io/a_gothic_gamebook/scenes/Sad_ending_-_AGG_2025'>Sad ending</a></h3>\n            <p>The quest has failed: their love could not prevail against ill fate. Rune is destined to wed the old bachelor, imposed by their tutor, while a life of misery and regret will attend Sasha… The lovers are parted for eternity.Musical pieces: Gretchen am Spinnrade D.118, Wie viele Zeit verlor Ich IHW 15 n. 37</p>\n            </body>\n            ",
